{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      EfficientDet-lite0 — Recommended ✦\n      Train EfficientDet-lite0 on the public CarDD dataset (Kaggle), convert to TF.js format, serve from /public/models/. Run inference on a 320×240 canvas frame every 1.5s during recording. WebGL backend (~30–50ms/frame), WASM fallback for devices without GPU support.\n      \n        Pros\n          ~4.4MB model — fast to load, fits in memory\n          No network calls during recording\n          Works offline / in tunnels\n          Easy to swap in fine-tuned model later (just replace the files)\n        \n        Cons\n          Needs one-time training run in Python (Keras + TF)\n          Accuracy limited by small model size on subtle damage","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1779693074592}
